From 9332878ba5a181d9f38de3034e62c3dc7802b922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Klemm <github@tklemm.eu>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:09:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Compare versions in a loop instead of zip

`Version#<=>` built `[0] * 6`, zipped both versions' parts into six more
arrays and returned from inside the block, which unwinds through `each`. A
`while` loop compares the same six positions in the same order and reads a
missing part as 0, as before. Rails' `allow_browser` compares the browser's
version with the minimum on most requests.

Callgrind instructions per `allow_browser` check over the same 21 user
agents, Ruby 4.0.9: 213,301 before and 207,471 after without JIT, 160,465
and 155,669 with YJIT, and 10 fewer objects.
---
 lib/user_agent/version.rb | 13 +++++++------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/user_agent/version.rb b/lib/user_agent/version.rb
index cba11bc..9df6d75 100644
--- a/lib/user_agent/version.rb
+++ b/lib/user_agent/version.rb
@@ -70,17 +70,18 @@ class UserAgent
       case other
       when Version
         if @comparable
-          ([0]*6).zip(to_a, other.to_a).each do |dump, a, b|
-            a ||= 0
-            b ||= 0
+          mine, theirs = to_a, other.to_a
+          i = 0
+          while i < 6
+            a = mine[i] || 0
+            b = theirs[i] || 0
+            i += 1
 
             if a.is_a?(String) && b.is_a?(Integer)
               return -1
             elsif a.is_a?(Integer) && b.is_a?(String)
               return 1
-            elsif a == b
-              next
-            else
+            elsif a != b
               return a <=> b
             end
           end
